{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCellsBridges","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCellsBridges","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityAArmLeg","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphy","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceAGeneral","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HoefsmitRep","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.WenzlWeightVanishing","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Hoefsmit","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.hecke_axialDistance_eq_unshifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.hecke_axialDistance_eq_unshifted","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L232-L243","doc":"The `+1` shift is a translation of both cells, so it cancels: the Hecke\naxial distance is the canonical one on the *unshifted* tableau coordinates.\nThis is what makes the shift a bookkeeping convention rather than a difference\nin the quantity being computed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.hecke_axialDistance_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.hecke_axialDistance_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L227-L230","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.hecke_axialDistance_eq_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.hecke_axialDistance_eq_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L220-L225","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.schurWeyl_axialDistance_eq_tableauContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.schurWeyl_axialDistance_eq_tableauContent","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L206-L211","doc":"The two duplicates are therefore equal to each other. This is the composite\nthat `QOU.SchurWeyl.axialDistance_eq_tableauContent` states directly; deriving it\nhere shows it is not special — it is what any two copies give. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.axialDistance_eq_tableauContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.axialDistance_eq_tableauContent","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L203-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.axialDistance_eq_schurWeyl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.axialDistance_eq_schurWeyl","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L200-L201","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.content_eq_jonesMarkovWenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.content_eq_jonesMarkovWenzl","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L192-L196","doc":"`JonesMarkovWenzl.cellContent` takes a partition it never uses (`_lam`,\nkept for call-site symmetry with `cellHookLength`). The bridge holds for every\npartition, which is the precise sense in which the argument is inert. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.content_eq_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.content_eq_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L189-L190","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.content_eq_qBetaWenzlWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.content_eq_qBetaWenzlWeight","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L186-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.content_eq_schurWeyl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.content_eq_schurWeyl","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L183-L184","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.hook_eq_hookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YoungDiagramCells.hook_eq_hookLength","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YoungDiagramCellsBridges.lean#L121-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@